0110: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0111:     """
0112:     Thicken the sparse frame and stamp the external sparse sprites into it in positional order.
0113: 
0114:     Input structure
0115:     The grid has a dominant background color, a regular lattice color, one large
0116:     sparse rectangular frame, and one or more external monochrome sprites whose
0117:     pixels also sit on a two-step lattice.
0118: 
0119:     Rule
0120:     Use the largest sparse rectangular perimeter as the frame. Clear that frame
0121:     region and the external sprite pixels to background, draw a solid one-pixel
0122:     border in the frame color, solidify each sparse sprite into its contiguous
0123:     two-step mask, and place the sprites inside the frame with equal gaps.
0124:     Wide frames receive sprites left-to-right by source position; tall frames
0125:     receive them top-to-bottom by source position.
0126: 
0127:     Key insight
0128:     The frame supplies ordered slots: the sprite-to-slot assignment is by visible
0129:     source order, not by numeric color or by matching individual cells.
