0008: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0009:     """
0010:     Dock two-tone sprites into color-matched horizontal bars with a color swap.
0011: 
0012:     Input structure:
0013:     - bg = most common color.
0014:     - Top area: small two-tone sprites (outer color + inner color).
0015:     - Below: horizontal bars spanning most of the row, each with a fill color and border color on edges.
0016: 
0017:     Rule:
0018:     - Match each sprite to the bar whose fill color equals the sprite's outer color.
0019:     - Place the sprite at its original x-position, aligned to the bar's bottom.
0020:     - Recolor: sprite outer → bar border, sprite inner → bar fill.
0021:     - Erase original sprites from the top area.
0022: 
0023:     Key insight: Color matching is inverted — the sprite's dominant color identifies its target bar, then gets swapped to the bar's accent color.
0024:     """
